commit_message:
Make it easier to traverse the HTMLMatcherGraph.

HTMLMatcherGraphNodes now return an absent FALSE edge is there isn't one. This makes it easier to write traversal code, which can do this:
  if (getNextNodeForEdgeKind(TRUE_EDGE).isPresent()) {
    traverse(getNextNodeForEdgeKind(TRUE_EDGE).get());
  }
  if (getNextNodeForEdgeKind(FALSE_EDGE).isPresent()) {
    traverse(getNextNodeForEdgeKind(FALSE_EDGE).get());
  }

Previously, traversal code had to check the type of the HtmlMatcherGraphNode and not attempt to get the FALSE_EDGE, because it was throwing an exception.
Tested:
  Updated unit tests as needed.

GITHUB_BREAKING_CHANGES=None.

